{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reload between a land check and its retry can omit required setup and wrongly block landing."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Replacing the limits table with a scalar silently changes active concurrency limits despite reporting that the section requires a restart."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Changing review mode before a restart can cause a resumed run to fail when it processes a cached panel review."}]}